The pure kernels, published so a stranger can run the gate

Rung 10 asks whether a didy can show a stranger the evidence without asking to
be believed. A green gate on the author's own laptop cannot answer that: it says
the gate passed on hardware the claimant controls, which is exactly the evidence
a stranger has no reason to accept.

So the kernels go out - pure logic, no credential, no memory, no seed - and
GitHub's runner clones them fresh and runs the same tag-pinned gate. That run is
the only thing in the whole ladder that does not rest on trusting the author.

164 mutants killed across seven kernels, 0 unexplained, 1 baselined with a
written proof of equivalence. CI fails on a surviving mutant and on any survivor
without a reason, because a gate that reports "not clean" and exits zero is
decorative.
